    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Tests, p-values, Errors & Power\"\ndescription: \"Understand hypothesis testing as a decision framework, visualize p-values, and simulate Type I error, Type II error and power.\"\nauthor: \"MLStation\"\ndate: 2026-10-01\ncategories: [Statistics, Hypothesis Testing, Inference]\ndraft: false\n---\n\n\nHypothesis testing is often taught as a ritual:\n\n```text\ncalculate p → compare with 0.05 → declare significance\n```\n\nThat hides the real structure.\n\nA test asks:\n\n> **If a specified null model were true, how surprising would data like these be?**\n\n::: {.callout-tip}\n## What you will learn\n- Null and alternative hypotheses\n- Test statistics and p-values\n- Type I and Type II errors\n- Statistical power\n- Why statistical significance is not practical importance\n:::\n\n## The p-value\n\nA p-value is the probability, **under the null model**, of observing a test statistic at least as incompatible with the null as the one observed.\n\nIt is **not** $P(H_0\\mid\\text{data})$.\n\n## Interactive: move the observed z-statistic\n\n```{ojs}\n//| echo: false\nviewof zobs = Inputs.range([0,4], {value:1.96, step:.05, label:\"|Observed z|\"})\nphi=z=>Math.exp(-z*z/2)/Math.sqrt(2*Math.PI)\ngrid=d3.range(-4.5,4.51,.02).map(x=>({x,y:phi(x),tail:Math.abs(x)>=zobs}))\ncdf=x=>0.5*(1+((z)=>{const t=1/(1+.3275911*Math.abs(z)); const y=1-(((((1.061405429*t-1.453152027)*t)+1.421413741)*t-.284496736)*t+.254829592)*t*Math.exp(-z*z);return z>=0?y:-y;})(x/Math.SQRT2))\npval=2*(1-cdf(zobs))\nhtml`<div class=\"ms-readout\"><span>Two-sided p-value</span><b>${pval.toFixed(4)}</b></div>`\n```\n\n```{ojs}\n//| echo: false\nPlot.plot({\n height:300,x:{label:\"z\"},y:{label:\"Null density\"},\n marks:[\n  Plot.areaY(grid.filter(d=>d.tail),{x:\"x\",y:\"y\",fill:\"#E11D48\",fillOpacity:.25}),\n  Plot.line(grid,{x:\"x\",y:\"y\",stroke:\"#4F46E5\",strokeWidth:2})\n ]\n})\n```\n\n## Errors are defined across repeated decisions\n\n| Reality | Do not reject $H_0$ | Reject $H_0$ |\n|---|---|---|\n| $H_0$ true | Correct | Type I error ($\\alpha$) |\n| $H_1$ true | Type II error ($\\beta$) | Correct; power $=1-\\beta$ |\n\n## Animation: power rises with effect size and sample size\n\n::: {#4032bf7c .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code code-fold=\"true\"}\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\nimport plotly.express as px\nfrom scipy.stats import norm\n\nrows=[]\nalpha=.05\ncrit=norm.ppf(1-alpha/2)\nfor n in [20,50,100,200,500]:\n    for d in np.linspace(0,0.6,61):\n        mu=d*np.sqrt(n)\n        power=norm.sf(crit-mu)+norm.cdf(-crit-mu)\n        rows.append({\"n\":n,\"effect\":d,\"power\":power})\ndf=pd.DataFrame(rows)\nfig=px.line(df,x=\"effect\",y=\"power\",animation_frame=\"n\",range_y=[0,1],\n            labels={\"effect\":\"Standardized effect size\",\"power\":\"Power\"})\nfig.add_hline(y=.8,line_dash=\"dash\")\nfig.update_layout(height=380)\nfig.show()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:380px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"788b2154-a996-4183-8de7-cd27d3ec215f\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"788b2154-a996-4183-8de7-cd27d3ec215f\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"788b2154-a996-4183-8de7-cd27d3ec215f\",                        [{\"hovertempl